  "name": "Jump Scare",
  "type": "feat",
  "img": "icons/magic/control/hypnosis-mesmerism-eye.webp",
  "system": {
    "description": {
      "value": "<p>A sudden jet of emotion causes your allies to suddenly act. If it is a linked foe's turn and they are frightened, you can spend a reaction and expend three link depth to allow an ally to immediately act as if it was their turn. During this extra turn, the selected ally has advantage on attack and damage rolls against the creature whose turn they interrupted and cannot willingly leave your aura. The linked creature resumes their turn after this extra turn concludes, and the selected ally skips their next turn.</p><p><a href=\"https://dnd-wiki.org/wiki/Empath_(5e_Class)\">Source: Empath by Axis, co-authored by Ghostwheel</a> (CC BY-SA 3.0). See the module's AUTOMATION.md for what is automated and how rules are interpreted.</p>",
      "chat": ""
    },
